     "seal",
     "bead",
     "Mesopotamia"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Harappans ate wheat, barley, peas, sesame, fish and meat, and used milk. They grew cotton for clothes.\nThey made beads, pots and metal tools. Traders used seals to mark goods and weights to measure them.\nThey traded with places like Mesopotamia and Oman by land and sea, exchanging beads, cotton and copper for other goods."
    }
